# Mercury Edit 2 — findings by Step 5 Preview (self-excluded: no verified public benchmark scores)

- Source: Inception Labs / `mercury-edit-2` (Inception Next Edit endpoint)
- Date: 2026-11-10 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Mercury Edit 2
- **Short description:** Inception Labs' purpose-built diffusion LLM (dLLM) for next-edit prediction — given recent snippets, the current file and edit history, it predicts the developer's next code edit and returns the updated editable region (Tab to accept). It is a specialized editor-prediction endpoint, not a general chat/reasoning model, and it complements Inception's auto-complete (FIM) endpoint. KTO preference training on human accept/reject feedback targets useful, selective suggestions.
- **Provider / access:** Inception Platform API (`https://api.inceptionlabs.ai/v1/edit/completions`, model `mercury-edit-2`, `inceptionai` SDK) plus editor integrations: Zed (edit prediction, one free month with the launch API key) and ProxyAI. No OpenCode Console/Zen route — verified absent from the live catalog.
- **Release / knowledge:** spec trackers (modelbenchmark.io, LLMDB) date it 2026-03-30; Inception's "Introducing Mercury Edit 2" blog post is dated 2026-10-29 (Zed integration launch). Knowledge cutoff not applicable/disclosed.
- **IDs:** `mercury-edit-2` (Inception API). No Free ID; new Inception API accounts automatically receive 10 million free tokens.
- **Context window:** conflicting sources — modelbenchmark.io's most-agreed host values (Inception + text-completion-inception) say **32K**; OpenRouter-sourced trackers (Serenities AI) say **128K**. Max output **8K** (both agree). Inception's own docs do not publish a window figure; for this endpoint the working set is 3–5 recently viewed snippets (~20 lines each) + the current file + the last 3–5 edit diffs.
- **Modalities:** text input, text output; no image/file input; no structured outputs documented; it is not a chat model (dedicated next-edit request format with `<|code_to_edit|>` / `<|cursor|>` markers).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-10):** $0.25 / 1M input, $0.75 / 1M output, $0.025 / 1M cached input (Inception; corroborated by two hosts on modelbenchmark.io and OpenRouter pricing on Serenities).
- **Architecture:** proprietary diffusion language model (parallel token generation, not sequential decoding); weights and parameter counts undisclosed.

### Raw benchmarks found

- Quality benchmark suite: Inception benchmarks on three open next-edit suites — Instinct, Fill-in-the-middle (HumanEval-infilling, test-case validated) and Next-edit Prediction (NEP) — plus one internal benchmark, averaged into a single quality figure, with LLM-as-a-judge scoring on three of them. **The absolute scores are not published** in the blog post or docs: every per-dimension row below would read "no verified public score found".
- The only measured claims, both relative to Inception's previous next-edit model (vendor-reported): edits are **accepted 48% more often**, and the model is **27% more selective** in the edits it displays.
- Speed: **~1,000 tokens/second decoding** (Inception docs), with a recommended editable region of 10–15 lines (~100–150 tokens) and a practical upper bound of ~250 tokens; end-to-end latency is measured by the vendor but not published as a number.
- Comparisons against custom next-edit models and speed-optimized frontier models are claimed ("superior quality and speed") without published figures.
- Terminal-Bench 2.1 / Tau3-Banking / GDPval-AA / Claw-Eval / Toolathon / MCP-Atlas: no verified public score found (not applicable to a specialist endpoint and never measured publicly).
- GPQA Diamond / HLE / LCR / CritPt / AA Intelligence Index / Omniscience: no verified public score found.
- SWE-bench Verified / LiveCodeBench / SciCode / Vibe Code Bench / DeepSWE / Coding Index: no verified public score found — FIM/NEP/Instinct are the relevant family and their values are unpublished.
- MRCR / RULER / GraphWalks long-context retrieval: no verified public score found.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

Not computed — self-exclusion. With zero verified public benchmark numbers for this exact model/ID (the four-benchmark quality average is described but never published, and the acceptance/selectivity figures are deltas against the prior model, not absolute scores), none of the five quality dimensions can be normalized without inventing values, so no `Overall Score` exists and this file stays `.excluded` (per `model-report-TEMPLATE.md` SELF-EXCLUSION and `RULES.md` permanence: one fabricated number would drag the mean for every reader).

- Tool use: no verified public score found
- Reasoning: no verified public score found
- Context window: no verified public score found (window itself disputed: 32K vs 128K across sources)
- Multimodal: no verified public score found (text-only by documentation)
- Coding: no verified public score found (specialty next-edit prediction; suite scores unpublished)
- Cost efficiency: no verified public score found ($0.25/$0.75 per 1M documented; 10M free starter tokens on new Inception accounts)
- Overall Score: not computable (zero verified published benchmark scores)

